  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186100869,
      "id": "b494140f-206a-5317-8079-ff719a253140",
      "title": "Determining Whether Two Matrices Are Conformable for Multiplication"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "27038c16-45c9-5470-a656-1cf9cfece954",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$P=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 2 & 9\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$R=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 7 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 9 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 6 & -4 & -3 & -3\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$S=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -5 & 4 & 7\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $P,R,$ and $S?$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $P$ is a $1\\times 3$ row vector, $R$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, and $S$ is a $1\\times 4$ row vector.\n\nThere are $4$ columns in $R$ and $1$ row in $S.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $S,$ the matrices $R$ and $S$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{4\\times 4}{\\times }_{\\ne }{S}_{1\\times 4}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $3$ columns in $P$ and $1$ row in $S.$ Since the number of columns in $P$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $S,$ the matrices $P$ and $S$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{P}_{1\\times 3}{\\times }_{\\ne }{S}_{1\\times 4}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $4$ columns in $S$ and $4$ rows in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $S$ equals the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $S$ and $R$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{S}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{R}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 4}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nThe product $SR$ is well defined. The products $RS$ and $PS$ are undefined.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "fe7681dd-446a-5a9f-b31d-33684a4e2df0",
          ":answer-field/key": "The product $RS$ is well defined.",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "26a85286-5c22-5d38-a148-1314c64a88a0",
