      ":question/problem": "<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$P=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -3 & -3 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$R=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 & -5 & 5 \\\\ 8 & 3 & -7 & -9 \\\\ -5 & 6 & -3 & 9 \\\\ 9 & 7 & -8 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$S=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -9 & -6 & 7\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $P,R,$ and $S?$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $P$ is a $1\\times 4$ row vector, $R$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, and $S$ is a $1\\times 4$ row vector.\n\nThere are $4$ columns in $R$ and $1$ row in $S.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $S,$ the matrices $R$ and $S$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{4\\times 4}{\\times }_{\\ne }{S}_{1\\times 4}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $4$ columns in $S$ and $4$ rows in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $S$ equals the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $S$ and $R$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{S}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{R}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 4}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $4$ columns in $P$ and $4$ rows in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $P$ equals the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $P$ and $R$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{P}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{R}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 4}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nThe products $SR$ and $PR$ are well defined. The product $RS$ is undefined.",
