    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "acb85070-2329-59ad-a62b-4b4ed428ef72",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$O=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -9 & -8 \\\\ -3 & 8 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 9 & -3\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$P=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$R=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & 9 & 8 \\\\ 6 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 8 & 5 & 8\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $O,P,$ and $R?$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $O$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix, $P$ is a $1\\times 3$ row vector, and $R$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\nThere are $3$ columns in $P$ and $3$ rows in $O.$ Since the number of columns in $P$ equals the number of rows in $O,$ the matrices $P$ and $O$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{P}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{O}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 3}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $3$ columns in $P$ and $3$ rows in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $P$ equals the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $P$ and $R$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{P}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{R}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 3}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $3$ columns in $O$ and $3$ rows in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $O$ equals the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $O$ and $R$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{O}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{R}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 3}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nThe products $PO$ and $PR$ and $OR$ are well defined.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "8b573ebe-1885-5202-a841-a0d9310b3473",
          ":answer-field/key": "The product $PO$ is well defined.",
