  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186100869,
      "id": "b494140f-206a-5317-8079-ff719a253140",
      "title": "Determining Whether Two Matrices Are Conformable for Multiplication"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "5c50e846-5bb9-5b1d-95b0-5eb6d2b375a5",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$P=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -3 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$R=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -8 & 6 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -4\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$S=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -8 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $P,R,$ and $S?$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $P$ is a $1\\times 3$ row vector, $R$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix, and $S$ is a $1\\times 3$ row vector.\n\nThere are $3$ columns in $P$ and $3$ rows in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $P$ equals the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $P$ and $R$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{P}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{R}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 3}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $3$ columns in $S$ and $3$ rows in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $S$ equals the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $S$ and $R$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{S}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{R}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 3}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $3$ columns in $R$ and $1$ row in $P.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $P,$ the matrices $R$ and $P$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{3\\times 3}{\\times }_{\\ne }{P}_{1\\times 3}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nThe products $PR$ and $SR$ are well defined. The product $RP$ is undefined.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "293f4472-bcfa-595b-b0a0-103baf90fbcd",
          ":answer-field/key": "The product $PR$ is well defined.",
