    "question": {
      ":question/id": "0592d01d-876f-503f-8c56-c5d8cf400558",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$L=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & 9\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$M=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -6 & -8 & 8 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$N=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $L,M,$ and $N?$\n\nI. The product $NL$ is well defined\n\nII. The product $NM$ is well defined\n\nIII. The product $LM$ is well defined",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $L$ is a $1\\times 2$ row vector, $M$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix, and $N$ is a $3\\times 1$ column vector.\n\nThere is $1$ column in $N$ and $1$ row in $L.$ Since the number of columns in $N$ equals the number of rows in $L,$ the matrices $N$ and $L$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{N}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{L}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there is $1$ column in $N$ and $2$ rows in $M.$ Since the number of columns in $N$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $M,$ the matrices $N$ and $M$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{N}_{3\\times 1}{\\times }_{\\ne }{M}_{2\\times 4}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $2$ columns in $L$ and $2$ rows in $M.$ Since the number of columns in $L$ equals the number of rows in $M,$ the matrices $L$ and $M$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{L}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{M}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 4}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statements I and III are true, while statement II is false.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "0165bf5c-3fff-5d38-9c79-bc308946e33a",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
