      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$P=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 8 & -5 & -6 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$R=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -9 & -6 & 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$S=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -8 \\\\ 1 & -2 \\\\ 7 & 8 \\\\ -5 & -8 \\\\ -4 & -5\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $P,R,$ and $S?$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $P$ is a $1\\times 5$ row vector, $R$ is a $1\\times 5$ row vector, and $S$ is a $5\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $5$ columns in $R$ and $5$ rows in $S.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ equals the number of rows in $S,$ the matrices $R$ and $S$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{5}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{S}_{\\boxed{\\text{5}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $5$ columns in $P$ and $5$ rows in $S.$ Since the number of columns in $P$ equals the number of rows in $S,$ the matrices $P$ and $S$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{P}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{5}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{S}_{\\boxed{\\text{5}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $2$ columns in $S$ and $1$ row in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $S$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $S$ and $R$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{S}_{5\\times 2}{\\times }_{\\ne }{R}_{1\\times 5}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nThe products $RS$ and $PS$ are well defined. The product $SR$ is undefined.",
