  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186100869,
      "id": "b494140f-206a-5317-8079-ff719a253140",
      "title": "Determining Whether Two Matrices Are Conformable for Multiplication"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "841056e9-bc4c-59e1-97c2-8c75e5083590",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$O=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 7\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$P=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -4 & -8 & 3 & -3 \\\\ -6 & -8 & 2 & -4 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$R=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 4 \\\\ -9 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $O,P,$ and $R?$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $O$ is a $1\\times 2$ row vector, $P$ is a $2\\times 5$ matrix, and $R$ is a $5\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nThere are $2$ columns in $O$ and $2$ rows in $P.$ Since the number of columns in $O$ equals the number of rows in $P,$ the matrices $O$ and $P$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{O}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{P}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 5}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $2$ columns in $R$ and $1$ row in $O.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $O,$ the matrices $R$ and $O$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{5\\times 2}{\\times }_{\\ne }{O}_{1\\times 2}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $5$ columns in $P$ and $5$ rows in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $P$ equals the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $P$ and $R$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{P}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{5}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{R}_{\\boxed{\\text{5}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nThe products $OP$ and $PR$ are well defined. The product $RO$ is undefined.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "61928a9a-d03a-5f53-9b89-04647906fe0a",
          ":answer-field/key": "The product $OP$ is well defined.",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
