    "question": {
      ":question/id": "e95ff174-acce-537a-8faf-a9ab93072476",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$P=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -8 \\\\ 5 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$R=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & 2 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$S=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -3 & -7 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $P,R,$ and $S?$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $P$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix, $R$ is a $1\\times 5$ row vector, and $S$ is a $1\\times 4$ row vector. \n\nThere are $4$ columns in $S$ and $4$ rows in $P.$ Since the number of columns in $S$ equals the number of rows in $P,$ the matrices $S$ and $P$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{S}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{P}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $2$ columns in $P$ and $1$ row in $S.$ Since the number of columns in $P$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $S,$ the matrices $P$ and $S$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{P}_{4\\times 2}{\\times }_{\\ne }{S}_{1\\times 4}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $5$ columns in $R$ and $1$ row in $S.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $S,$ the matrices $R$ and $S$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1\\times 5}{\\times }_{\\ne }{S}_{1\\times 4}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nThe product $SP$ is well defined. The products $PS$ and $RS$ are undefined.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
