  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186100869,
      "id": "b494140f-206a-5317-8079-ff719a253140",
      "title": "Determining Whether Two Matrices Are Conformable for Multiplication"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "7424ed78-7704-5691-a0dd-9c3c5950ad70",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$P=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -7\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$R=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 3 & 7 & 3 \\\\ -7 & -7 & -4 & -9 \\\\ 8 & -4 & 9 & -8\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$S=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -1 & -6\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $P,R,$ and $S?$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $P$ is a $1\\times 3$ row vector, $R$ is a $3\\times 4$ matrix, and $S$ is a $1\\times 3$ row vector.\n\nThere are $3$ columns in $S$ and $3$ rows in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $S$ equals the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $S$ and $R$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{S}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{R}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 4}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $3$ columns in $P$ and $3$ rows in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $P$ equals the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $P$ and $R$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{P}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{R}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 4}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $4$ columns in $R$ and $1$ row in $P.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $P,$ the matrices $R$ and $P$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{3\\times 4}{\\times }_{\\ne }{P}_{1\\times 3}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nThe products $SR$ and $PR$ are well defined. The product $RP$ is undefined.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "1d40ba03-8201-5fce-96df-c327b3442b66",
          ":answer-field/key": "The product $SR$ is well defined.",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "2f1119dd-a0ae-5e1a-ba6e-45e76a4cca82",
