    "question": {
      ":question/id": "44527d60-440d-5424-9a09-dbdcc54e1e3e",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$O=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 9 & -4 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$P=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 1 & -7 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 7 & 7 \\\\ -5 & -3 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -8 & -8 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 6 & -9 & -8\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$R=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 & 8 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 9 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -4 & -5 & -8 & 0 \\\\ -9 & -7 & -3 & -4 & -9\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $O,P,$ and $R?$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $O$ is a $1\\times 5$ row vector, $P$ is a $5\\times 4$ matrix, and $R$ is a $4\\times 5$ matrix.\n\nThere are $5$ columns in $O$ and $5$ rows in $P.$ Since the number of columns in $O$ equals the number of rows in $P,$ the matrices $O$ and $P$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{O}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{5}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{P}_{\\boxed{\\text{5}}\\times 4}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $4$ columns in $P$ and $4$ rows in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $P$ equals the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $P$ and $R$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{P}_{5\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{R}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 5}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $5$ columns in $R$ and $5$ rows in $P.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ equals the number of rows in $P,$ the matrices $R$ and $P$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{4\\times \\boxed{\\text{5}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{P}_{\\boxed{\\text{5}}\\times 4}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nThe products $OP$ and $PR$ and $RP$ are well defined.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "5ec26633-077f-57dd-88db-4cb81fbf41da",
