  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186100869,
      "id": "b494140f-206a-5317-8079-ff719a253140",
      "title": "Determining Whether Two Matrices Are Conformable for Multiplication"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "b3ebe2ed-0b19-5139-91e1-75485433f503",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$P=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 2 & -6\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$R=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 6 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$S=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 3 & -4 & -6 & 9 \\\\ -6 & 0 & 7 & -5 & -9 \\\\ -7 & 8 & -2 & 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $P,R,$ and $S?$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $P$ is a $1\\times 3$ row vector, $R$ is a $1\\times 3$ row vector, and $S$ is a $3\\times 5$ matrix. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $R$ and $3$ rows in $S.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ equals the number of rows in $S,$ the matrices $R$ and $S$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{S}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 5}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $5$ columns in $S$ and $1$ row in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $S$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $S$ and $R$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{S}_{3\\times 5}{\\times }_{\\ne }{R}_{1\\times 3}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $3$ columns in $P$ and $3$ rows in $S.$ Since the number of columns in $P$ equals the number of rows in $S,$ the matrices $P$ and $S$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{P}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{S}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 5}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nThe products $RS$ and $PS$ are well defined. The product $SR$ is undefined.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "f50bbfac-5ed0-565e-b8e3-0a96395477d1",
          ":answer-field/key": "The product $RS$ is well defined.",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "e5df0f8a-41a0-5205-9178-19ca19ff7e28",
