    "question": {
      ":question/id": "324cddbe-e03d-570e-8220-a2c35b58d5ba",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$P=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -1 & 0 & 9 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$R=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 8 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -5 & -9 \\\\ 8 & 6 & 9 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 8 & -1 & -7 \\\\ -9 & 0 & 6 & -8\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$S=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 1 & -2 & 5 & -7\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $P,R,$ and $S?$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $P$ is a $1\\times 5$ row vector, $R$ is a $5\\times 4$ matrix, and $S$ is a $1\\times 5$ row vector.\n\nThere are $5$ columns in $S$ and $1$ row in $P.$ Since the number of columns in $S$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $P,$ the matrices $S$ and $P$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{S}_{1\\times 5}{\\times }_{\\ne }{P}_{1\\times 5}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $5$ columns in $S$ and $5$ rows in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $S$ equals the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $S$ and $R$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{S}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{5}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{R}_{\\boxed{\\text{5}}\\times 4}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $5$ columns in $P$ and $5$ rows in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $P$ equals the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $P$ and $R$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{P}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{5}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{R}_{\\boxed{\\text{5}}\\times 4}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nThe products $SR$ and $PR$ are well defined. The product $SP$ is undefined.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
